# walk.ts

- Two phases: `collectBlocks` builds descriptors, `materialize` renders them. Never render inside the walk.
- Every descriptor needs `sourceStart`/`sourceEnd`. Import blocks also need `statementStart`/`statementEnd`.
- Inline comments attach via `statements.at(-1)!.commentText`, guarded by `statements.length > 0`. There is no `lastBlock` variable. Keep the guard; never index without it.
- `at(-1)` is the last descriptor, not the last rendered block. `drive.settings()` expands to several descriptors.
- `docstringConsumed` is set by every non-comment statement. Do not reset it mid-body.
- Mutator blocks: call `loadExtraState({ taskCount })` before `initSvg()`, or the inputs do not exist yet.
- `getMultitaskComments` matches arguments by **start offset** against `getCallArgumentNodes`, not by node-type counting. Keyword args (`race=True`) are three separate `ArgList` children, so counting node types misaligns every later comment. Do not refactor to node-type counting. See AGENTS.md.
- `materialize` measures `getBlocksBoundingBox()` before creating each block. Keep that order.
- Literal args go in `fields` under the input name and land on the `math_number` shadow via `applyFieldValue`.
- Unmapped constructs must fall back to `pybricks_raw_code`. Never drop a statement.
- `fixtures/robot.py` and `fixtures/exampleattach.py` must stay at zero raw blocks (`src/acceptance.test.ts`).
